      "missing_expression": "The melee-strike-spawns-icy-projectiles identity lands as a two-geometry composite (melee_strike + multi_projectile) with GEOMETRY_PROPAGATION_cascade for the hit-to-fan propagation, but the engine expresses it as two discrete geometries rather than a single unified 'strike that emits a projectile fan' primitive.",
      "proposed_fix_target": null,
      "proposed_fix_type": "none",
      "source_anchor": "The melee-strike-spawns-icy-projectiles identity lands as a two-geometry composite (melee_strike + multi_projectile) with GEOMETRY_PROPAGATION_cascade for the hit-to-fan propagation, but the engine expresses it as two discrete geometries rather than a single unified 'strike that emits a projectile fan' primitive. The 30%-less-damage fan and the exact 'behind the first target' spawn geometry are behavioral properties. A player keeps the engage-in-melee / damage-projects-behind feel; the tight coupling of one attack producing both hits is generalized to two linked geometries."
    }
  ],
